The `save_data` function does not properly null-terminate the string before writing it to the destination buffer. If the user inputs more than 200 characters, it could lead to a buffer overflow, potentially allowing an attacker to overwrite adjacent memory locations.

To fix this issue, you should add a null terminator after copying the data into the buffer:
```rust
fn save_data(dest: &mut [u8], src: &String) {
    if src.chars().count() > INPUT_SIZE {
