### 3. **Unrestricted Shell Access**
When accessing the configuration panel, the program executes `/bin/sh` with inherited standard input/output streams. This allows an attacker to execute arbitrary commands on the host machine if they manage to reach this part of the application.

Consider implementing additional checks or restrictions when executing shell commands, such as limiting command execution to specific files or directories only.

